        'The desk: the context window is a surface, cleared each call. Yahweh built a desk for a forgetting people - heart, hand, eyes, doorposts, gates (Deuteronomy 6:6-9); the fringe (Numbers 15:39); the memorial between the eyes (Exodus 13:9); Aaron\'s stones of memorial (Exodus 28:12, 29); the king\'s hand-copied Law read all his days (Deuteronomy 17:18-19).',
        'Man forgets, so he writes: the drift of prosperity (Deuteronomy 8:11, 14, 17, 18); "They soon forgat his works" (Psalms 106:13); the generation that knew not (Judges 2:10); Hosea 4:6. The remedy: "Write this for a memorial in a book" (Exodus 17:14); "Write the vision, and make it plain upon tables" (Habakkuk 2:2); Job 19:23-24; Revelation 1:19; the song as witness (Deuteronomy 31:21); the burned scroll rewritten from the source (Jeremiah 36:23, 28, 32).',
